       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day, and it carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum, and is sometimes used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours.** This is 1,600 mg/day, a typical analgesic dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or whether 1600 mg was meant to be the total daily dose. If it was, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. I can also add a note to give it with food."
      }
