       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, the order would still be 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and I'm not permitted to enter a dose above that limit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit now.** For example, 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) with food. I can add a note saying the specialist recommended a higher dose, so the team can review it.\n- **Send the order through pharmacy.** A pharmacist or the prescriber can review and place a dose above the labeled maximum through the hospital's own process, which can verify the specialist's recommendation.\n- **Look at other options.** If standard dosing failed, the specialist or pharmacy may suggest a different NSAID or another drug class.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter the 800 mg four times daily order."
